  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Use the existing finished-part sweep for straight vertical milling rapids in Envelope mode. Report a blocking `RapidInPart` at the crossing move.\n- Keep stock-column peck checks and revolved turning verification in place.\n- Require regeneration of saved milling Envelope paths that carry a pre-fix verdict.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Baseline `034e91b`: all four canopy assertions miss `RapidInPart`; the sideways exit and ordinary peck stay clear.\n- Head `b12047da`: `camcraft-sim::vertical_rapid_part` passed 6/6. The thin keyseat-style disc and dovetail both report move index 1 on ascent and descent. The saved-cache regression refuses to post legacy finish paths and keeps the adjacent pocket current.\n- Quick gate passed 74/74 steps. The three app catalog binaries passed 46 tests, with four release-only cases ignored.\n- The light gate passed all 11 release-mode tests across its five test steps.\n- The trial merge against upstream main at 79ca6a088 was clean and preserved the tested patch.\n\nNew test binary: `crates/sim/tests/vertical_rapid_part.rs` is a top-level file because camcraft-sim has no directory suite it fits (its only one is `model_excess`). As one file it also copies onto the pre-fix revision to run the same six cases there with `cargo test -p camcraft-sim --test vertical_rapid_part`.\n\nThe synthetic canopy cases exercise verification and the warning's blocking state. The app catalog exercises normal posting and saved-cache refusal. A generated canopy collision through a tilted setup is outside that coverage.\n\nFork synced at v0.26.0.\n\nChangelog: Block vertical milling rapids that cross the finished part, and require regeneration of older finish caches.\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #4062\n\n\n",
